// expect: 7 (the run half waits on Hβ.lower.list-rest-binding-runtime)
// mn-lambda-list-param — the lambda list-pattern parameter (PLAN §11
// Phase 3.3's first measured drift): `([h, ...t]) => h` is SYNTAX's own
// documented form («Destructuring patterns in param position»), and
// `fn f([h, ...t])` already parses — the lambda path failed because the
// paren content parses as an EXPRESSION first and `...` was not
// expression grammar. The cover-grammar rest (RestExpr, minted by the
// list parser, consumed by expr_to_pat, loud anywhere else) closes the
// second-weaker-copy gap without a second parameter parser. The
// frontier leg gates the PARSE half (no parse diagnostic at check, and
// the one coverage verdict the pattern owes: a parameter pattern is an
// arm on the argument, and this one leaves `[]` untaken); the
// RUN half is the named peer's gate — the rest BINDING emits a
// hand-baked $make_list call reachability cannot see, so solo emission
// dangles (measured at pin 8031eaf1).
fn pick(f, xs) = f(xs)

fn main(q) = pick(([h, ...t]) => h, [7, 8, 9])
